From ec79563a7f4bc9141030b228125cc3b0e785429e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:56:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grate: spill fragment temporaries to surface 4

Shaders whose live values exhaust the scalar register file were refused.
Use all four register rows and retry allocation with scalar spilling when
ordinary allocation runs out of registers.

Follow NVIDIA's T30 ST_R20/LD_R20 sequence, retaining clean backing slots
until a value is overwritten or dies. Reserve the store/load scratch
registers, preserve spill operations during row layout and blending, and
allocate the context's surface-4 backing from the program's slot count.
Scalarize independent lanes and pack independent ALU work on the retry
path. Reject programs exceeding one 64-step epoch without aborting.

Checked against NVIDIA compiler output and GPU replays, an independent
CPU model at 200x150 and 1024x768, and the installed driver. Automatic
spill tests are exact or within 1/255, including source-over blending.
The regression suite passes 24 tests with one expected 3D-texture skip.
Interleaved tex/alu/coord benchmarks remain within observed variation.
Cross-built with ninja -j12 and formatted with the driver's clang-format.
